  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "A modulating signal <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>t</mi></math> is added to the carrier signal <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;for amplitude modulation. The combined signal is passed through a non-linear square law device. The output is then passed through a band pass filter. The bandwidth of the output signal of band pass filter will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>MHz</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Frequencies present in output of square law device</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub></math></p><p>After passing through band pass filter, frequencies present&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub></math></p><p>Bandwidth of the output signal <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MHz</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
